{
  "id": "relative-sensitivity",
  "term": "relative sensitivity",
  "definition": "Relative sensitivity is the degree to which one assessment model or measure is more responsive than another to symptoms or differences in psychopathology. In this context, it means comparing personality measures by how well they detect symptoms of personality disorders and non-personality disorders.",
